From 19166c2221d9e4e5c02e03f73a6cb39cbb339f6c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ondrej Jirman <megi@xff.cz>
Date: Thu, 6 Aug 2026 23:26:29 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Revert "media: sun6i-csi: Take the bus width from the format
 when there is no endpoint"

This reverts commit 337e6d1c5183a.

The premise was wrong. The pattern source does get a bus width:
sun6i_csi_pattern_s_stream() sets the endpoint's from the configured
mbus code, and has since the generator became a source in the graph. So
the interface was already being widened to twelve bits when a twelve bit
format was selected, and the fallback added by that commit could never
fire for the source it was written for.

What the twelve bit capture showed was therefore the truth about the
hardware rather than a driver limitation: with the bus genuinely twelve
bits wide, the generator still supplies eight, left justified.

Signed-off-by: Ondrej Jirman <megi@xff.cz>
---
 .../sunxi/sun6i-csi/sun6i_csi_bridge.c        | 49 +------------------
 .../sunxi/sun6i-csi/sun6i_csi_bridge.h        |  6 ---
 2 files changed, 2 insertions(+), 53 deletions(-)

